WEBVTT

00:07.240 --> 00:10.670
Good morning, strangers.

00:10.670 --> 00:15.040
I am Ka Grava Rai Fuu Gramstahl.

00:15.040 --> 00:16.580
You're...

00:16.580 --> 00:19.080
The Undead Merchant?

00:19.080 --> 00:22.580
Hm, indeed.

00:22.580 --> 00:26.520
Now then, why don't you both join me for breakfast...?

00:26.520 --> 00:28.790
Sounds good, yes?!

00:30.460 --> 00:34.300
Can you please be a bit quieter?

00:34.300 --> 00:38.700
Even with your Wu Xing Ti, my fists are capable of destroying you from the inside.

00:38.700 --> 00:40.370
P-Please wait!

00:40.370 --> 00:44.210
We came here to speak with you about Red Dragon!

00:44.210 --> 00:47.140
The name of our country is Nil Kamui.

00:47.140 --> 00:49.310
It's a small island country.

00:49.310 --> 00:54.080
The covetous, great ancient country of Kouran conducted a sudden invasion

00:54.080 --> 00:57.120
and plundered a third of the land.

00:57.120 --> 01:00.260
Our ally, the great country to the east, D'natia,

01:00.260 --> 01:04.660
defended settlements where they had their bases, then kept silent.

01:04.660 --> 01:07.760
The two great countries quickly carved away Nil Kamui's lands

01:07.760 --> 01:11.500
like meat from a sacrificial swine.

01:11.500 --> 01:18.240
Our guardian deity, Red Dragon, didn't protect the land.

01:18.240 --> 01:21.080
Imperial Era 3015, September...

01:21.080 --> 01:25.250
Our country was no longer ours.

01:25.250 --> 01:30.020
<i>The heat-haze shimmers, ember-toned</i>

01:30.020 --> 01:34.460
<i>Its blurred afterimage far away</i>

01:34.460 --> 01:36.580
<i>(I'm back in this life)</i>

01:47.370 --> 01:56.710
<i>My shout added to the noise</i> <i>and disappeared into the chaos</i>

01:56.710 --> 01:57.710
<i>(Don't wait)</i>

01:57.710 --> 01:59.810
<i>One single life I choose to end</i>

01:59.810 --> 02:02.880
<i>In every breath I take it ends</i>

02:02.880 --> 02:05.120
<i>One single life I choose to end</i>

02:05.120 --> 02:07.320
<i>In every breath I take it ends</i>

02:07.320 --> 02:11.560
<i>Defiling even this chosen fate</i>

02:11.560 --> 02:17.800
<i>With the blood of judgment</i>

02:17.800 --> 02:23.300
<i>"If I can just solve this unraveling</i> <i>moment with my own hands"</i>

02:23.300 --> 02:28.380
<i>I howled enough to burn my life out</i>

02:28.380 --> 02:34.050
<i>I left my hopes to an</i> <i>undependable past and vanished</i>

02:34.050 --> 02:39.650
<i>Cruelly enough, my voice was beautiful</i>

02:39.650 --> 02:43.690
<i>The ending world</i>

02:43.690 --> 02:48.560
<i>I'll be a judgment light</i>

03:01.280 --> 03:03.240
And you folks are?

03:03.240 --> 03:06.880
Huh? Can't you make an educated guess?

03:06.880 --> 03:10.920
Ah, nice to meet you! My name is Shaddy, and this here is Sol.

03:10.920 --> 03:15.020
We came here to greet you by order of Lord Ka Grava.

03:15.020 --> 03:17.760
Are you both Bound Ones?

03:17.760 --> 03:19.230
Shaddy is.

03:19.230 --> 03:22.200
Sol is a human-monster half-breed.

03:22.200 --> 03:23.900
He's a Mixed One.

03:23.900 --> 03:27.800
A Bound One and a Mixed One are acting as messengers for the Undead Merchant?

03:27.800 --> 03:32.540
Yes! Lord Ka Grava treats everyone without discrimination!

03:32.540 --> 03:33.980
Oh...?

03:33.980 --> 03:35.910
Stop with this prattle.

03:35.910 --> 03:39.910
We need to hurry so that we're not found by the Kouran forces surrounding the city.

03:39.910 --> 03:43.950
Ah! I'm so sorry! Sol is always like this.

03:43.950 --> 03:46.320
Um, let's go to the city for now, shall we?

03:46.320 --> 03:47.810
Okay.

03:50.460 --> 03:52.550
I'm sorry to disturb you.

03:54.260 --> 03:57.930
This better be worth waking me up...

03:57.930 --> 03:59.400
Yes!

03:59.400 --> 04:01.940
Well, Ka Grava...

04:01.940 --> 04:03.100
He was asleep?!

04:03.100 --> 04:04.900
Yes! Over there...

04:14.580 --> 04:20.750
During the one month we surrounded him, that tin can was sleeping all along?!

04:23.760 --> 04:26.420
Lord Ka Grava!

04:27.630 --> 04:30.860
--Lord Ka Grava!
--Lord Ka Grava!

04:34.800 --> 04:37.360
Ta-daaaa!

04:48.950 --> 04:51.290
Lord Ka Grava!

04:51.290 --> 04:53.290
They're here!

04:53.290 --> 04:57.890
Oh? So you're members of the combined expedition, yes?

04:57.890 --> 04:59.730
Now, come on board!

04:59.730 --> 05:03.130
Let's have a nice chat at my manor!

05:04.630 --> 05:07.840
Finally shows up, eh?

05:07.840 --> 05:12.830
Today's the day I'm gonna get back at you for making a fool out of me!

05:22.550 --> 05:23.750
Gotcha!

05:23.750 --> 05:26.420
I killed Ka Grava!

05:26.420 --> 05:30.860
We're gonna crush Haiga by force before D'natia intervenes!

05:30.860 --> 05:32.360
Yes!

05:32.190 --> 05:33.920
"Haiga \ Ka Grava's manor"

05:46.510 --> 05:50.380
The overhaul took one whole month, and now look!

05:53.750 --> 05:56.620
--Shaddy!
--Alley-oop!

06:01.960 --> 06:03.860
Well, now, I kept you waiting!

06:03.860 --> 06:09.530
I must say, Gakusho shows great taste in aiming for my costliest part!

06:09.530 --> 06:12.030
Gakusho, as in the Kouran general?

06:12.030 --> 06:17.210
Why, yes! She was hailed as a master sniper during the Seven Year War.

06:17.210 --> 06:22.540
She seems to have a grudge against me, even after I sold her guns and gunpowder.

06:24.410 --> 06:28.250
There's no sense having all these guns if we don't have the gunpowder for them!

06:28.250 --> 06:32.650
The price for gunpowder has been inflating in Nil Kamui and even in our country!

06:32.650 --> 06:35.560
There's no doubt that Ka Grava is cornering the market!

06:35.560 --> 06:36.890
That bastard!

06:36.890 --> 06:41.560
He inflated the price of gunpowder after he sold the guns for cheap!

06:44.570 --> 06:46.100
--Retreat!
--Y-Yes!

06:46.100 --> 06:48.760
He's gonna pay for this...!

06:51.110 --> 06:54.840
Kouran's forces will lay siege to this city,

06:54.840 --> 06:57.410
believing that you're helping to fund the revolutionary army.

06:57.410 --> 07:03.850
Hm... It seems it will be difficult to maintain Haiga's neutral position.

07:03.850 --> 07:07.120
This is the current image of Haiga's main gate.

07:07.120 --> 07:09.990
Looks like Kouran's pride, the steam tank brigade, is in position...

07:09.990 --> 07:13.130
I doubt even Haiga's walls would hold more than a day.

07:13.130 --> 07:18.430
It seems Kouran is going on the offensive, knowing that D'natia is closing in.

07:18.430 --> 07:19.770
I know!

07:19.770 --> 07:22.870
After battle commences in the city, we can draw D'natia's forces in,

07:22.870 --> 07:29.040
and once confusion arises among the forces, we can just assassinate both of their leaders!

07:30.280 --> 07:32.310
Nah, that's, you know...?

07:32.310 --> 07:34.720
I do think it's the simplest approach.

07:34.720 --> 07:39.220
No! We need to find a way to prevent this without hurting anyone!

07:39.220 --> 07:40.790
For example?

07:40.790 --> 07:44.230
Why not speak with them once more?

07:44.230 --> 07:46.960
Ibuki, it's a bit too late for that, don't you think?

07:46.960 --> 07:50.870
Certainly! I think that idea's fine, too.

07:50.870 --> 07:52.670
If we speak with them, I'm sure they'll listen...

07:52.670 --> 07:55.570
Hm... Well, how about this, then, Ibuki?

07:55.570 --> 07:59.040
If you're able to avoid this battle through negotiation,

07:59.040 --> 08:03.570
then I'll acknowledge you as being worthy to hear Red Dragon's message.

08:08.020 --> 08:09.820
Lord Ka Grava?

08:09.820 --> 08:12.220
You're there, aren't you?

08:12.220 --> 08:14.590
Oh? What is it, Lou?

08:14.590 --> 08:19.060
I wanted to give you some information regarding Ibuki.

08:19.060 --> 08:20.090
Oh?

08:20.090 --> 08:23.760
He holds mysterious powers as a Child of Contract.

08:23.760 --> 08:30.270
Yes... He has the power to kill anyone in front of him in exchange for the life of another.

08:30.270 --> 08:34.910
Hm... And that's why you agreed with Ibuki's idea?

08:34.910 --> 08:38.540
That's a harsh way to "negotiate," though.

08:39.550 --> 08:42.280
It's all for him to decide...

08:44.020 --> 08:46.020
I'll go, even if I have to go by myself.

08:46.020 --> 08:50.420
Oh, no! One person alone isn't enough to carry the burden.

08:50.420 --> 08:53.060
Then, I'll go with him.

08:53.060 --> 08:55.200
Take this with you.

08:55.200 --> 08:56.560
This is...?

08:56.560 --> 08:59.300
It's my letter of apology to Gakusho.

08:59.300 --> 09:00.400
Apology?

09:00.400 --> 09:03.400
Yes, an apology for the one month I've been asleep.

09:03.400 --> 09:09.640
In any case, if an Imperial takes this letter of apology to her, I'm sure she'll at least listen.

09:09.640 --> 09:12.210
I'd like to avoid war, too.

09:12.210 --> 09:16.220
I hope that you will be able to find a way to get through to her.

09:16.220 --> 09:18.320
Yes!

09:18.320 --> 09:23.160
That's the spirit, Ibuki! Spirit! Spirit!

09:24.160 --> 09:28.800
I see... So this is what you were preparing for, Lou...

09:28.800 --> 09:30.060
Yes...

09:30.060 --> 09:34.270
If he uses that power again,

09:34.270 --> 09:38.610
we may be able to determine the true nature of Red Dragon's power.

09:38.610 --> 09:41.580
We must investigate them thoroughly.

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
"Wu Xing Ti \ Kouran created many mysterious

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
arts and items, but none so strange as

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
the Wu Xing Ti, a technique allowing

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
the replacement of human parts. This technique

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
was said to be born from the research of

09:44.950 --> 09:48.680
eternal life and was very costly to maintain."

09:50.480 --> 09:53.250
Lou Chun Wah, this is as far as you will go.

09:53.250 --> 09:56.690
And to think I guided him here...

09:56.690 --> 09:58.460
Scary, scary...

09:58.460 --> 10:01.600
I'll save you no matter what happens.

10:01.600 --> 10:05.200
I won't abandon my friend.

10:05.200 --> 10:06.790
I'll be going.

10:17.310 --> 10:22.220
I heard Ka Grava's messenger was a descendant of the Imperials, but all we got was a kid.

10:22.220 --> 10:23.840
That sword...

10:47.310 --> 10:50.750
Now, no one can bother us.

10:50.750 --> 10:52.240
Come in.

10:54.420 --> 10:56.520
We'll have to ask you to enter alone.

10:56.520 --> 10:58.990
I'll be waiting.

10:58.990 --> 11:00.480
Remember that.

11:08.530 --> 11:11.530
I'm not big on formalities with my superiors.

11:11.530 --> 11:12.900
They scare me!

11:12.900 --> 11:15.040
Oh, hush...

11:15.040 --> 11:21.770
Besides, we need to buy as much time as possible while Ibuki is in negotiation.

11:23.210 --> 11:25.780
I'm the one who wants to sigh...

11:23.710 --> 11:26.710
"Haiga outskirts \ D'natia force's camp site"

11:26.880 --> 11:28.950
Hello?

11:28.950 --> 11:31.690
Um, I'm looking for a certain person...

11:31.690 --> 11:34.180
Where is Lady Ulrika?

11:36.390 --> 11:38.430
So we finally meet...

11:38.430 --> 11:41.430
...Sir Sweallow Clazzvali.

11:41.430 --> 11:46.530
I'm the acting subleader for the third corps of the Black Dragon Knights, Ulrika Ledezma.

11:49.440 --> 11:54.710
I'm the Leader of One Thousand,
General Seisha of Kouran, Gakusho.

11:54.710 --> 11:56.380
My name is Ibuki.

11:56.380 --> 12:00.720
I bring to you a letter from
Ka Grava Rai Fuu Gramstahl.

12:00.720 --> 12:01.920
What...?

12:01.920 --> 12:03.320
It's a letter of apology from Ka Grava.

12:03.320 --> 12:05.120
Ka Grava?!

12:08.960 --> 12:12.130
Wh-What are you doing?!

12:12.130 --> 12:15.160
Stop this farce at once.

12:15.160 --> 12:19.300
I'm only meeting you because you're an Imperial.

12:19.300 --> 12:22.100
Are you really going to attack Haiga?

12:22.100 --> 12:23.800
Can't you tell?

12:23.800 --> 12:26.670
I need to crush the source of the revolutionary army's funds.

12:26.670 --> 12:30.580
Even so, you're going to kill innocent people just for that?!

12:30.580 --> 12:34.180
I lost a lot of comrades myself.

12:34.180 --> 12:37.850
Even General Kohkaku, who took good care of me.

12:37.850 --> 12:40.450
This will even everything out, kiddo.

12:42.320 --> 12:45.190
I wonder if Ibuki has noticed by now...

12:45.190 --> 12:48.860
Gakusho has no intention of reading my letter...

12:48.860 --> 12:52.000
...and is in no way willing to talk.

12:52.000 --> 12:53.170
In other words, he...

12:53.170 --> 12:55.870
...only has one choice...

12:55.870 --> 12:59.440
He needs to kill Gakusho to stop the war.

12:59.440 --> 13:05.810
With her gone, the remaining soldiers and
D'natia's forces won't be fighting in Haiga.

13:07.110 --> 13:12.320
So what? Don't you have anything else up your sleeve, Imperial kiddo?

13:12.320 --> 13:16.460
Ka Grava and the others knew this was going to happen from the beginning...

13:16.460 --> 13:19.560
Is killing her my only choice...?

13:19.560 --> 13:24.570
But in order to do that, I need to offer a friend to the dragon again...

13:24.570 --> 13:26.800
But that's...!

13:29.340 --> 13:31.700
What's with that look of yours?!

13:34.070 --> 13:35.980
--Wha--?!
--Eykha!

13:35.980 --> 13:37.210
Ibuki!

13:37.210 --> 13:39.040
That other brat?!

13:40.880 --> 13:43.020
You savages are out of your minds!

13:43.020 --> 13:44.650
Shoot me.

13:46.220 --> 13:48.390
Shoot me with that.

13:48.390 --> 13:50.420
Eykha...?

13:50.420 --> 13:56.500
Just like Kohkaku, you will be scorched by the dragon's flame, Gakusho.

13:56.500 --> 13:59.230
What is she saying...?

13:59.230 --> 14:00.700
Hurry!

14:00.700 --> 14:03.740
If you kill me, Gakusho will die too.

14:03.740 --> 14:07.040
But... But you're...

14:08.180 --> 14:10.210
...not my friend!

14:10.210 --> 14:12.710
Killing me will determine that.

14:12.710 --> 14:14.780
Wait!

14:14.780 --> 14:18.520
If she dies, I'll die?

14:18.520 --> 14:22.760
Is that how they were able to defeat the general?

14:22.760 --> 14:26.560
Gakusho is aware of General Kohkaku's demise.

14:26.560 --> 14:31.270
That will lead her to believe in the power that Ibuki holds.

14:31.270 --> 14:35.470
So, doubt begets doubt.

14:35.470 --> 14:37.440
What should I do?

14:37.440 --> 14:40.600
Do you seek power, Imperial?

14:46.210 --> 14:47.310
No!

14:47.310 --> 14:52.590
If my flames are what you desire, then offer me an equivalent.

14:52.590 --> 14:54.090
Ibuki?

14:54.090 --> 14:55.620
No...!

14:55.620 --> 14:57.590
I don't want to kill anyone!

14:57.590 --> 15:01.500
Killing others won't solve anything!

15:01.500 --> 15:03.500
He's serious...

15:03.500 --> 15:06.100
He seriously thinks he can kill me.

15:06.100 --> 15:07.300
Ibuki!

15:07.300 --> 15:11.240
There... There has to be a way!

15:11.240 --> 15:12.970
Ka Grava?!

15:12.970 --> 15:17.110
The overhaul took one whole month, and now look!

15:17.110 --> 15:20.450
He inflated the price of gunpowder...

15:20.450 --> 15:23.950
It's my letter of apology to Gakusho.

15:23.950 --> 15:26.440
Stop this farce at once.

15:27.920 --> 15:29.260
I see!

15:29.260 --> 15:32.350
She thinks Ka Grava died...

15:33.690 --> 15:38.860
In that case, notifying her that he's alive may lead me to a different choice!

15:41.970 --> 15:45.170
General Gakusho, I beseech you!

15:45.170 --> 15:47.140
Please read that letter!

15:47.140 --> 15:51.110
That was written by
Ka Grava himself! He's alive!

15:51.110 --> 15:52.610
What...?

15:52.610 --> 15:56.180
Even if he's some machine,
I shot him in the head...

15:56.180 --> 16:00.450
Wait... Could he truly be, as his name suggests, undead?

16:00.450 --> 16:02.060
You know what to do!

16:02.060 --> 16:05.460
Please, if you want to save yourself, listen to me!

16:06.560 --> 16:07.960
What now...?

16:07.960 --> 16:12.500
If Ka Grava is alive, there's room to negotiate, but...

16:12.500 --> 16:14.400
After she reads the letter, then what...?

16:14.400 --> 16:16.170
What's to negotiate...?

16:16.170 --> 16:21.170
But if this isn't done, I'm going to end up killing Eykha and Gakusho...

16:22.310 --> 16:24.080
Bring it, now!

16:24.080 --> 16:25.570
Y-Yes!

16:27.010 --> 16:30.320
The stamp looks authentic...

16:30.320 --> 16:32.820
But...

16:32.820 --> 16:36.090
I see now... That shrewd bastard!

16:36.090 --> 16:38.860
It's no use conducting a war after seeing this!

16:38.860 --> 16:40.760
Um, excuse me?

16:40.760 --> 16:42.500
Isn't it a letter of apology...?

16:42.500 --> 16:45.100
Apology?

16:45.100 --> 16:47.230
It's a peace treaty!

16:47.230 --> 16:50.370
I've got no complaints with the conditions written here.

16:50.370 --> 16:51.860
Then...!

16:59.010 --> 17:01.550
Send word to our forces!

17:01.550 --> 17:04.250
Haiga has accepted our demands!

17:04.250 --> 17:09.360
Moving forward, we will enter
Haiga as an occupying force!

17:09.360 --> 17:13.050
Be forewarned that if there are any rioters,
I'm gonna drill them full of holes!

17:16.300 --> 17:20.200
Ka Grava must have set something up...

17:20.200 --> 17:21.900
During my sleep...

17:21.900 --> 17:25.710
No, during my overhaul, an unfortunate misunderstanding has occurred,

17:25.710 --> 17:27.910
and for that, I would like to apologize.

17:27.910 --> 17:31.950
It was definitely not my intention to dismiss your advancement.

17:31.950 --> 17:36.050
The government of Haiga will stop any further resistance

17:36.050 --> 17:39.720
and will regrettably accept abidance under the rules of Kouran's security.

17:39.720 --> 17:44.430
In addition to the costs of being stationed here,
I will provide the expected concessions.

17:44.430 --> 17:47.660
I look forward to your sound and right decision...

17:47.660 --> 17:49.500
Stationed...?

17:49.500 --> 17:50.930
That's right...

17:50.930 --> 17:56.100
I don't mind fighting, but killing and plundering isn't my thing.

17:56.100 --> 17:59.910
I have a personal grudge against Ka Grava, but...

17:59.910 --> 18:02.440
...for now, I'll forget about that.

18:02.440 --> 18:04.140
Thank goodness...

18:04.140 --> 18:06.750
Well, if you'll excuse us.

18:06.750 --> 18:07.920
Just a sec, Ibuki.

18:07.920 --> 18:09.450
Huh?

18:09.450 --> 18:13.320
At least you're different from the other spineless savages.

18:13.320 --> 18:14.320
Wha--?!

18:14.320 --> 18:17.320
Ibuki is going to become king of this island.

18:17.320 --> 18:20.490
Looks like you're going to be one tough king to deal with!

18:23.300 --> 18:26.030
Thank you very much.

18:26.030 --> 18:28.940
Speaking strictly of results, killing Gakusho

18:28.940 --> 18:31.710
or sealing the negotiation by having her read the letter...

18:31.710 --> 18:35.780
Those were the only two choices you had from the very beginning.

18:35.780 --> 18:39.680
The latter choice was very difficult to achieve based on the situation,

18:39.680 --> 18:45.190
but even when you were at a loss, you held to your ideal to the very end.

18:45.190 --> 18:47.050
Ibuki...

18:47.050 --> 18:51.860
I will acknowledge you as a person worthy of imparting my knowledge to.

18:51.860 --> 18:56.630
But the result was Haiga being occupied by Kouran...

18:56.630 --> 19:00.130
I'm merely having them stationed here for security purposes.

19:00.130 --> 19:02.900
Besides, Kouran isn't the only one who will be stationed here.

19:02.900 --> 19:04.370
Huh?

19:04.370 --> 19:08.410
D'natia's ambassador should arrive shortly.

19:08.410 --> 19:10.540
Who is this ambassador?

19:10.540 --> 19:14.150
Oh, someone you know very well.

19:14.150 --> 19:16.220
Sweallow...?

19:16.220 --> 19:18.050
Kouran and D'natia...

19:18.050 --> 19:21.920
By bringing them in at the same time, the balance of powers can be kept...

19:21.920 --> 19:26.560
I guess we were all manipulated by you all along...

19:26.560 --> 19:29.260
But this is just a temporary fix.

19:29.260 --> 19:33.170
Their forces led me to surrender Haiga's independence.

19:33.170 --> 19:35.040
This is fact.

19:35.040 --> 19:38.270
That's about all a petty merchant can do.

19:38.270 --> 19:40.040
Now then, can you gather everyone?

19:40.040 --> 19:43.780
As promised, I'll talk about Red Dragon.

19:43.780 --> 19:45.270
Yes!

19:47.210 --> 19:50.840
And I did have a promise with Red Dragon...

19:52.220 --> 19:57.950
To help the Imperial that would, one day, come in search of me.

20:02.200 --> 20:05.530
Why didn't you kill me?

20:05.530 --> 20:07.300
Is it because I'm not your friend?

20:07.300 --> 20:10.600
Or is it because I am your friend?

20:10.600 --> 20:15.610
You're... my friend, Ibuki.

20:15.610 --> 20:17.100
Th...

20:18.250 --> 20:21.080
Thank you...

20:21.080 --> 20:24.050
Now then, Red Dragon, was it?

20:24.050 --> 20:27.250
I have a message from him.

20:27.250 --> 20:29.290
A message from Red Dragon?

20:29.290 --> 20:33.430
But before that, we need to listen to Eykha's story.

20:33.430 --> 20:34.560
Me?

20:34.560 --> 20:39.430
Yes, about the revolutionary army's first expedition...

20:39.430 --> 20:43.100
...that was destroyed while attempting to hunt Red Dragon, who went mad.

20:44.270 --> 20:45.840
Eykha...

20:45.840 --> 20:49.180
That's right... I didn't talk about that.

20:49.180 --> 20:53.480
Maybe I wanted to forget about it...

21:07.630 --> 21:14.130
Izun was the leader of the first expedition, and a Bound One bonded with a Stone Giant.

21:14.130 --> 21:18.940
He initially thought he could persuade Red Dragon.

21:40.790 --> 21:44.200
That's Red Dragon...?

21:46.000 --> 21:46.470
"Act 4"

21:47.400 --> 21:50.700
"Act 4 \ Amid Enemies"

21:57.640 --> 22:02.880
<i>The end I thought I'd chosen;</i> <i>though the melody may warp (more)</i>

22:02.880 --> 22:07.850
<i>At last the pounding heartbeat</i> <i>desires it and performs</i>

22:07.850 --> 22:13.090
<i>Both the evened-out impulse</i> <i>and the wiped-out lament (now)</i>

22:13.090 --> 22:19.560
<i>Are wings that race onward,</i> <i>tearing through the fog</i>

22:32.910 --> 22:42.860
<i>Emotions that can't be hidden in words</i> <i>that push people away (bleeding through)</i>

22:42.860 --> 22:48.060
<i>Emptying both hands so I can get what I want</i>

22:48.060 --> 22:55.560
<i>If I can't even find fault</i> <i>with this unshrinking expanse</i>

22:56.770 --> 22:58.310
<i>What am I supposed to believe?</i>

22:58.310 --> 23:02.480
<i>I need nothing if I have you:</i>
<i>That alone is enough</i>

23:02.480 --> 23:12.480
<i>Go on and cry: You burn so bright because</i> <i>the gears of transmigration are turning</i>

23:12.620 --> 23:22.620
<i>Tightly spin together the intertwining roads</i> <i>to which your shouts led you</i>

23:27.000 --> 23:27.470
"Act 5"

23:27.070 --> 23:29.970
Act 5: "In a Fog."

23:29.970 --> 23:37.080
The undead revived from the abyss stand in the way of those seeking Red Dragon.

23:37.080 --> 23:40.810
Is there no place where one can gain happiness?!
